pi.github.com/users/nesb1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-18T06:16:36Z","updated_at":"2025-08-18T06:16:36Z","body":"@kdn36 I looked at how aggregation works. I want to suggest getting rid of the possibility of inconsistency between `groups` and `state` in the `AggregationContext` struct, however, I may not understand something.\n\nThere are situations in the code when the `state` changes, then the `groups` change (except `AggregatedScalar`). There are also situations in the code when only `groups` change, for example, during filtering, when data has not been aggregated, while these changes are not reflected on the state, that is, on the series. This is the first part of the problem.\n\nThe second part of the problem is the use of the `flat_naive` function, which is very dangerous in terms of bugs, even though its name says so. I also noticed that this function can be replaced with `get_values`, so it is sometimes used where there can be no nested values.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pola-rs/polars/issues/comments/3195270713/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"nesb1","id":41860443,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxODYwNDQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41860443?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1","html_url":"https://github.com/nesb1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nesb1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://ap